    "summary": "`bench`'s three jobs (`bench`, `record`, `record-25k`) no longer build each side in a worktree. The head's, the base's and the reference's binaries come from `ci/native/store.sh fetch \u2026 release`, into each tree's `native/bin/`. A `profile` of `breach_tick_phases` runs its `profiling` key. A key that isn't stored is built once and uploaded, so a run builds the head at most, and nothing when the head's `native/` tree is already stored. Profiling any other tool still builds it in place, because the store keeps only `tick_phases`' profiling build. Each job now has `contents: write` (to upload) and `GH_TOKEN`/`GH_REPO`.",
    "title": "chore(bench): take every side's binaries from the native store"
